# j2j Spring Boot Starter Kit — project memory

## Stack

Spring Boot 4.1.0 · Java 25 · PostgreSQL · JetMoonlight `jet:2.1.0`

## Integration

- JetMoonlight auto-configures via classpath — **no** `@ComponentScan("com.jet.moonlight")`
- Single HTTP entry: `WebActionsController` → `dispatchSafely()`
- Example service: `AuthService` with `@MarkedAsJetService(name = "auth")`
- Security SPI: `SpringSecurityJetContext` implements `JetSecurityContext`
- Docs: JetMoonlight auto-injects `/docs` + `/docs/openapi.json`; blank `jet.docs.token` is public; `JwtFilter` skips docs paths
- Secrets: never commit JWT keys, docs tokens, `.env`, credential JSON, or keystores; use `JWT_SECRET` / `JET_DOCS_TOKEN`

## Auth flow (optimized)

1. `JwtFilter` — one `loadUserByUsername` per Bearer request
2. `JwtUtility.isTokenValid(token, user)` — uses loaded user, no second DB read
3. `UniversalService.authenticatedUser()` — reads `SystemUserModel` from `SecurityContext`, no DB

## Removed / migrated

- Local AOP handlers (`@Required`, `@Can`, …) — moved to JetMoonlight
- `NativeQueryHelperService` — deleted (unused)
- GCP object storage (`spring-cloud-gcp-starter-storage` and credentials JSON) — removed
- Mail auto-config is opt-in (`jet.mail.enabled`, default `false`)

## Domain layer

- `UniversalService` — auth, roles, domains, field validation helpers
- JPA helpers under `models/jpahelpers/`
- Repositories under `repositories/`

## Agent checklist

- [ ] New features = new `@Action` methods, not new controllers
- [ ] Use JetMoonlight security annotations, not custom AOP in this repo
- [ ] No per-request filter logging
- [ ] Rebuild JetMoonlight JAR if library API changed
